cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Loupe, please cite it as below."
title: "Loupe: a closer look at AI-written chip designs that pass their tests"
abstract: >-
  Strict re-scoring of LLM-generated Verilog on RTLLM v2.1 and VerilogEval v2.
  Each official testbench pass gets a formal proof class against the reference
  design (unbounded proof, bounded only, proved wrong, unknown). Pre-registered
  and timestamped with OpenTimestamps (Bitcoin block 972099) before scoring.
authors:
  - family-names: Venugopal
    given-names: Jishnu
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jishnuvenugopal/loupe"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
keywords:
  - LLM evaluation
  - Verilog
  - formal verification
  - benchmarks
  - reinforcement learning
